@description ReaPackLab: centrally managed REAPER package manager
@author ReaLab
@version 0.14.5
@changelog
  Restore valid local url.txt priority; hosted recovery only for missing, unreadable or invalid local pointers.
  Do not switch configuration after a selected local URL download or configuration validation fails.
  Bound full-scan retries to a new launch, revision change or explicit Force Scan; retain five-minute policy checks.
  Rename Force Sync action/menu label to Force Scan, preserving its existing command ID.
  macOS 15.0+ Apple Silicon (ARM64). Developer ID-signed, hardened runtime and Apple notarized.
@provides
  [darwin-arm64] reaper_reapacklab-arm64.dylib https://github.com/rockumk/ReaPackLab/releases/download/v$version/$path
@link
  Distribution repository https://github.com/rockumk/ReaPackLab
  Source code https://github.com/rockumk/ReaPackLabDev
@about
  # ReaPackLab

  ReaPackLab is a fork of ReaPack designed for managed REAPER environments.

  This package provides a Developer ID-signed and Apple-notarized macOS 15.0+
  Apple Silicon binary. It is the centrally managed edition, not the separate
  ReaPackLabSetup bootstrap extension. Test downloaded builds in an isolated
  REAPER resource directory before classroom deployment. Restart REAPER after
  installing or updating a native extension.

  Based on ReaPack by Christian Fillion (LGPL-3.0-or-later).
